            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chelsey Wylde"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used pecans instead of walnuts, and added a splash of orange juice before adding the flour. After I baked the cookies, I dipped the bottom into white chocolate. They baked into not too thin and not too thick cookies that stay soft. I did not refrigerate my dough.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-02T17:13:04.593Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SinnedRachel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used zest from mandarin oranges and added a 1/2tsp dried lavender flowers. Otherwise I followed the recipe exactly. The cookies turned out fluffy and chewy. I'm a crunchy fan 100%! Some had more of a salt flavor than others. I'm going to get this right eventually!",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-04T18:46:10.753Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "vwshelb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Variation: used lemon vest instead of orange. Formed into \"logs\", after cool dipped bottom in white chocolate and 1/2 bath in milk chocolate disks. Chopped walnuts very fine in food processor and folded into dough. Great flavor, will definitely try again with orange zest. Great cookie!",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-07T11:51:06.393Z"
